# mods.manifest — authoritative mod set for ModSentry policy enforcement.
# Source of truth: valheim-mods/SERVER-HANDOFF.md (Ethan's handoff). Byte-exact DLLs
# are in ./dll/, verified against these SHA-256 pins. If ./dll/<dll> is absent,
# stage-mods.sh downloads the pinned Thunderstore zip and extracts+verifies the DLL.
#
# Format:  name | version | dll | sha256 | role | url
#   role: plugin (loaded on server) / required / optional (ModSentry policy refs).
#         combine with '+', e.g. plugin+required
# BepInEx pack (denikson 5.4.2333) is installed by the lloesche image (BEPINEX=true).
# Client and server DLLs must be byte-identical or ModSentry kicks the client.
#
# GOTCHA — Thunderstore / r2modman search is fuzzy and badly ranked: the mod you
# want is often NOT the first hit (or even on the first page). Exact-name queries
# still surface near-duplicates, forks, and unrelated packages above the real one,
# so scroll a few results and confirm the author + package before trusting a URL.
# Verify you grabbed the right one by matching the author/package in the url below
# (e.g. NightOfGames/Huginn_Map, not some other "Huginn"), not just the mod name.
#
# ============================================================================
# VALHEIM 1.0 (l-1.0.7, network v39, Unity 6) — mod status
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1.0 broke the pre-1.0 mods (Jotunn 2.29.2 crashed on client connect via the
# removed field ZRoutedRpc.Everybody; GlassPieces threw a client TypeLoadException).
#
# 2026-09-10: Jotunn shipped 2.30.0 and Drop That shipped 3.1.5 (both 1.0 builds),
# so both are RE-ENABLED below.
#
# 2026-09-10 (later): re-tested the three still-disabled mods on their EXISTING
# versions now that Jotunn 2.30.0 is a 1.0 build — none shipped a new version, but a
# Jotunn-dependent mod could load on its current build if Jotunn was its only blocker.
# Loaded all three server-side and read BepInEx LogOutput.log. Result:
#   * FarmGrid 1.0.0    -> RE-ENABLED. Loads clean under Jotunn 2.30.0 (no TypeLoad /
#       Harmony / dependency errors). Jotunn was its only blocker. Client-side/optional.
#       (Server-side load verified from the headless server; its build-placement grid
#        overlay is a client UI feature and was not exercised on a real client.)
#   * Huginn Map 1.0.5  -> STAYS DISABLED. It now LOADS ("Huginn active"), but its own
#       code calls game internals that 1.0 removed/renamed, so its headline features are
#       broken: shared map data fails (Method not found Minimap.ReadExploredArray) and
#       boat tracking fails (Field not found ZoneSystem.m_activeArea). Jotunn being fixed
#       only un-blocked loading; Huginn itself needs a 1.0 rebuild.
#   * GlassPieces 1.2.5 -> STAYS DISABLED. Still throws TypeLoadException (VTable setup
#       of GlassPieces.Functions.Collector/SliderSwitch) on 1.0. It depends ONLY on
#       BepInEx, not Jotunn, so the Jotunn update never applied to it — needs a rebuild.
#
# 2026-09-10: evaluated Favorite_Items (Valheazy) for the pack as an optional client mod.
# DISABLED — broken on 1.0. It loads and reads its config, but its FixedUpdate throws a
# TypeLoadException every physics tick ("Could not resolve type ... expected class 'Element'")
# — it references an inventory-UI type 1.0 removed/renamed. A missing-type error like this is
# independent of runtime state, so it fails on clients too, not just the headless server.
# Deps only BepInEx; needs a real 1.0 rebuild. Listed below (commented) so check-mod-updates
# flags it when Valheazy ships a new version.
#
# Re-enable Huginn/GlassPieces/Favorite_Items — un-comment, bump version+SHA, re-stage, rebuild
# the client pack, restart — once each ships a real 1.0 build. Track with ./check-mod-updates.sh.
# Disabled DLLs are preserved on the VM under /srv/valheim/config/_disabled_mods_20260909/.
#
# WARNING: do NOT leave DropThat's WriteDropTablesToFiles (drop_that.cfg [Debug]) enabled.
# On 1.0 it pegs all game threads on world start and (on the old 3-core VM) starved the
# guest agent, requiring a hard reset. Enable it briefly to dump prefab ids, grab the
# files from BepInEx/Debug/, then set it back to false. (Jotunn 2.30.0 itself is fine.)
# ============================================================================
ModSentry|1.0.17|Landoria.ModSentry.dll|3737e773d53c9eff761e5db84b4940a41c359e87fa5c7d57949da27b317aa027|plugin+required|https://thunderstore.io/package/download/Landoria/ModSentry/1.0.17/
Drop_That|3.1.5|Valheim.DropThat.dll|9b4c1718932f48eb2d1fe8e50973dccb53e9947bc5f9903b87d3da05ab5efaf4|plugin+required|https://thunderstore.io/package/download/ASharpPen/Drop_That/3.1.5/
Jotunn|2.30.0|Jotunn.dll|51d32cfbe2db5c203ffb8855c155d185d572dda72db49066905679d8ec5e3c46|plugin+required|https://thunderstore.io/package/download/ValheimModding/Jotunn/2.30.0/
